---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import CodeExample from "../../components/CodeExample.astro";
import PageIntro from "../../components/PageIntro.astro";
import { SITE } from "../../consts";
import lessonSource from "../../generated/examples/tutorial-functions.kwe?raw";

const source = lessonSource.trimEnd();
const output = "30\nOkenye\nNwatakịrị\nAda\nefu";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Lesson 5: Functions and Return Values"
  description="Learn named Kwechiri functions, parameters, calls, return values, and current function rules."
>
  <PageIntro
    eyebrow="Tutorial 05"
    title="Functions and Return Values"
    lead="Declare reusable named functions, accept parameters, call them, and return values with laghachi."
    meta="Beginner · Complete Lesson 4 first"
  />

  <div class="shell content-layout">
    <nav class="docs-nav" aria-label="Tutorial navigation">
      <a href="/tutorials/repetition-and-loop-control/">← Lesson 4: Repetition and Loop Control</a>
      <a href="/tutorials/functions-and-return-values/" aria-current="page">Lesson 5: Functions and return values</a>
      <a href="/tutorials/arrays-and-objects/">Lesson 6: Arrays and objects</a>
      <a href="/tutorials/modules/">Lesson 7: Modules</a>
    </nav>
    <article class="prose">
      <h2>The program</h2>
      <p>Open <code>examples/tutorials/functions.kwe</code>.</p>
      <CodeExample label="examples/tutorials/functions.kwe" code={source} output={output} />

      <h2>Run it</h2>
      <pre><code>node dist/cli/index.js examples/tutorials/functions.kwe</code></pre>

      <h2>Defining and calling</h2>
      <p>A named function starts with <code>ọrụ</code>:</p>
      <pre><code>ọrụ gbakọọ(a, b) &#123;
    laghachi a + b
&#125;</code></pre>
      <p>
        <code>a</code> and <code>b</code> are parameters available only inside
        the function. Call it with arguments:
      </p>
      <pre><code>nsonaazụ = gbakọọ(10, 20)</code></pre>

      <h2>Returning values</h2>
      <p>
        <code>laghachi</code> returns a value immediately and exits the whole
        function:
      </p>
      <pre><code>ọ bụrụ (afọ &gt;= 18) &#123;
    laghachi "Okenye"
&#125;
laghachi "Nwatakịrị"</code></pre>
      <p>
        Both reachable returns produce strings, so the inferred return type is
        string. A function that reaches the end without <code>laghachi</code>
        returns <code>efu</code>, which is why <code>kelee("Ada")</code> prints
        <code>Ada</code> and then returns <code>efu</code>.
      </p>

      <h2>Current rules</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Declare functions at module top level before calling them.</li>
        <li>Use the exact number of arguments.</li>
        <li>The first call establishes one parameter signature for the function.</li>
        <li>Every later call must use that same signature.</li>
        <li>Parameters and locals cannot capture module variables.</li>
        <li>Recursion, nested functions, closures, default parameters, and first-class functions are unsupported.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Your turn</h2>
      <p>
        Add <code>bipụta(gbakọọ(2, 3))</code> and predict the result. Then call
        <code>kọwaa</code> with a number below <code>18</code> and explain which
        <code>laghachi</code> supplies the result.
      </p>

      <div class="callout callout--gold">
        <strong>Common problems</strong>
        Declare the function before the call, use the exact argument count,
        return one concrete type across reachable paths, and remember that
        fallthrough returns <code>efu</code>.
      </div>

      <h2>Normative references</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><a href={`${SITE.github}/blob/main/docs/language-spec/functions.md`}>Functions</a></li>
        <li><a href={`${SITE.github}/blob/main/docs/language-spec/variables.md`}>Variables</a></li>
        <li><a href={`${SITE.github}/blob/main/docs/language-spec/errors.md`}>Current language errors</a></li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Next</h2>
      <p>
        Continue with
        <a href="/tutorials/arrays-and-objects/">Lesson 6: Arrays and Objects</a>.
      </p>
    </article>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
